# SSOP SYNTHETIC-SIGNAL injector — standing purple-team cadence.
#
# Fires fabricated MITRE-shaped signals (T1046 scan, T1053.005 task,
# T1071.001 HTTP exfil, T1566.001 phishing, T1572 DNS tunnel) directly into
# the live Wazuh alerts index using NEVER-tuned rule ids, so the router sweep
# mints fresh cases and the analyst/supervisory timers complete the chains
# into IRIS. Fixed doc ids -> re-runs overwrite, never duplicate.
#
# *** These are FABRICATED ALERTS, not adversary telemetry. ***
# Nothing on any host executes anything. This unit is named
# `ssop-synthetic-signals` (renamed from the misleading `ssop-atomic` on
# 2026-09-30) precisely so nobody reads it as Atomic Red Team. It was never
# Atomic Red Team; the old name invited that assumption and it was wrong.
# Real atomic execution is unbuilt — see wayfinder ticket
# `atomic-red-team-real-execution`.
#
# Cadence: every 30 minutes, offset from the router sweep (which runs every
# 3 min) so injected signals get picked up on the next sweep. Cost: ~1s of
# writes + the downstream chain. The 5 rules are fresh (9910xx/9915xx) so
# no tuning collision; if a supervisory deny ever auto-tunes them, the
# injector's fixed ids still land but dispatch goes silent — check the
# tuning ledger before assuming the pipeline is broken.
[Unit]
Description=SSOP synthetic-signal injector (30m; fabricated alerts, executes nothing)

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* *:0/30:00
Persistent=true
RandomizedDelaySec=60

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
